"Artona I, called the Mother or the Mother Planet, is the Artonans' original home world."
"Artona I has a demon problem that is only 'contained-ish'."
"An Artona I passport is needed to travel to Moon Thegund."
"Consulate instructors teach Earth classes from Artona I by screen, with no lag."
"Knights of the Mother Planet are an Artonan order young wizards aspire to join."
"Ships carrying wizards from the Mother answer chaos outbreaks on nearby worlds such as Thegund."
"Artona I has seasonal swarms of giant crabs."
"Artona I's Contract, Contract I, has a kernel called Mother who calls Artonans her children."
"Messages from Artona I reach Moon Thegund with almost an hour of delay."
"Instructor Gwen-lor's school on the Mother teaches wizard children from Year One to Year Six."
"Knights are released in a snowy forest stadium of tiered, mirror-polished wooden benches."
"There the Primary releases knights who choose their rest; tree roots draw their bodies down."
"The released knights' authority is woven into that ground and forest as a ward against chaos."
"Its largest continent is shaped like a 'diving num', with the first Rapport in its far north."
"Vethedya, the Artonan capital, is on Artona I."
"Allegiant villages live under one wizard's protection; moves between wizards are Here-to-Theres."
